  "description": "The political science major equips students to study the complexities of justice and power while developing analytical and communication skills applicable to many fields, including government, law, business, and the nonprofit sector. The major is intended to help students understand the world more deeply—going beyond partisan, national, and ideological divisions—and resolve to take action as faithful servants of Christ. Overlap Policy This program may not be combined with the international relations major, international relations minor, or politics, philosophy, and economics major.",
